**Full-stack Developer (PHP/React)**

**location:** world
**format:** full-time
**salary:** from 3500$ gross

**Firebird** is an international online travel company that organizes trips to Europe for customers from around the world. We have a dedicated software development department that focuses on our products that allow everyone else to deliver some of the top-notch, worldwide services. Currently, there are a number of commercially available projects in production that are being actively worked on:

- Service for booking rail tickets
- Online trip builder
- Service for booking hotels

**Tech stack **
PHP 8+ / Drupal, React / Next.js, MariaDB, Docker, Git 

Our product team is growing, and we’re looking for an experienced **Full-stack Developer**.
**
Your tasks will include**
- Designing and creating end-to-end project architecture — from data model and API design to UI/UX implementation;
- Backend development: PHP/Drupal services, business logic, custom modules;
- Frontend development: React/Next.js applications, component architecture, state management, SSR/SSG rendering strategies;
- Analysis of business requirements and design of their implementation across the full stack;
- Modification, implementation and creation of custom Drupal modules and themes, as well as reusable React components;
- Building responsive, accessible, and performant user interfaces;
- Integration with external services (Payment systems, Salesforce, GDS services, etc.) — both API-level integration and the corresponding UI flows;
- Participating in API contract design between backend and frontend;
- Conducting code reviews across backend and frontend codebases;
- Active use of Company-approved AI development tools (e.g., Cursor) in compliance with internal policies, security standards, and evolving corporate guidelines;
- Work with version control systems;
- Work in Jira, Confluence.

**Candidate requirements**
- 5+ years of experience shipping both backend and frontend features in production;
- Strong knowledge of PHP (>8.0): OOP, code refactoring, coding standards;
- Strong knowledge of React: hooks, component design patterns, state management (Redux/Context/Zustand);
- Hands-on experience with server rendering (Next.js) — SSR, SSG, ISR, API routes, hydration;
- Experience with at least one popular PHP framework (Drupal/Laravel/Symfony);
- Solid understanding of REST/GraphQL API design and backend-frontend integration;
- Understanding how web servers work; experience with Nginx + php-fpm;
- Experience with modern frontend tooling (Webpack/Vite, npm/yarn); TypeScript is a plus;
- Experience coding with AI agents (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex);
- Comfortable working in the Linux console;
- Experience with Git and code review workflows;
- Strong communication skills, comfortable working across backend and frontend concerns.
**
We offer**
- Competitive compensation based on interview results;
- Opportunity to build a stellar career in a fast-growing international travel company;
- Opportunity to work with advanced top-of-the-line software for travel management;
- Interesting, challenging tasks and a world-class team.

